(footprint "DFB1550LP_Butterfly14_Mech"
	(version 20241229)
	(generator "gen_dfb_fp.py")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Thorlabs DFB1550LP 14-pin butterfly laser - MECHANICAL PLACEMENT AID, NO PADS. The package is held in an Azimuth 5253-100-7S + -7R ZIF socket pair and is never soldered, so it has no land pattern; this footprint is board_only and exists to position the two sockets, the heat spreader cutout and the fiber exit. GEOMETRY from Thorlabs DOC-102831 Rev A p.3 (drawing rasterised - the PDF text layer does not identify which dimension is which). AXES: rotated 90 deg CCW from the datasheet top view so the lead rows run along Y at 2.54 mm pitch, matching the Azimuth socket footprints exactly - place JZ1 (S) at -X and JZ2 (R) at +X, both at rotation 0, and lead-to-contact alignment in Y is automatic. Body 12.70 mm across the lead rows x 20.80 mm along the fiber axis; lead rows exit at X = +/-6.35; 7 leads per row at Y = +7.62 .. -7.62. PIN 1 and PIN 14 are both at the FIBER end (+Y): pins 1-7 run down the -X row from Y=+7.62, pins 8-14 run up the +X row to Y=+7.62. Mounting flanges carry 4x Ø2.7 mm holes at X=+/-4.45, Y=+/-13.0 (8.9 mm across x 26.0 mm along) - these are for screwing the package to a heat spreader, they are NOT PCB holes and are drawn on F.Fab/User.Drawings only. HEIGHTS (front view): body 7.3 mm tall, baseplate flange 1.0 mm thick, LEAD PLANE 4.0 mm above the baseplate bottom. The Azimuth contact plane is 7.62 mm above the PCB face, so the butterfly baseplate bottom lands 7.62 - 4.00 = 3.62 mm above the board - that is the gap the heat spreader must close. NOT DIMENSIONED ANYWHERE IN THE DATASHEET: the free lead length beyond the body, and hence the socket-to-socket separation. The leads here are drawn 12 mm long as an indicative length only. MEASURE the free lead length L on the physical package, then set each socket so its odd-contact column (5.33 mm inboard of its datum edge) falls within the engaged lead, keeping the Azimuth 3.81 mm minimum engagement. Flange outer edge at Y=+/-14.6 is approximate - not dimensioned. Fiber boot Ø5.8 exits +Y for 24.0 mm; respect the fiber bend radius beyond that. 3D model is the Thorlabs STEP in SpecSheets - its origin/orientation against this footprint is UNVERIFIED.")
	(tags "thorlabs dfb1550lp butterfly 14-pin laser mechanical placement aid no-pads azimuth zif")
	(attr board_only exclude_from_pos_files exclude_from_bom)
